  "issue_date": "2025-10-31",
  "report_week": "44",
  "report_period": "Week 44 (24th Oct to 31st Oct 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Korea Line Corp have committed their Capesize \"Rosemary\" 179/2010 Daewoo, Korea (SS 04/2030, DD 05/2028) to Far Eastern interests at USD 28,5 mill. Note that a week ago, the one-year-younger \"Mineral Subic\" 179/2011 Hanjin, Korea (SS/DD 05/2026) was sold at USD 30,25 mill. The Kamsarmax \"Fjeld Saga\" 82/2013 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 08/2030, DD 09/2028) of Fjeld Shipping was committed to clients of ADS Maritime at USD 20 mill. For comparison, the two-years-older sister vessel \"Generosity\" 83/2011 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 05/2028, DD 11/2026) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 17 mill. Dryships committed their Panamax \"Majorca\" 74/2005 Hudong-Zhonghua, China (SS 11/2027, DD 12/2025, Scrubber fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 7,5 mill. Remind you that earlier this month, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Atheras\" 74/2006 Hudong-Zhonghua, China (SS 09/2026, DD 10/2025) was sold at USD 8,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, Kumiai Senpaku committed the \"KN Future\" 58/2013 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 10/2028, DD 11/2026) to Asian interests at USD 18,75 mill. For reference, the three-years-older sister vessel \"Forever SW\" 58/2010 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 05/2030, DD 04/2028) was sold in October at USD 15,2 mill. Moreover, the OHBS \"Atacama Queen\" 51/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026) of NS United Kaiun was committed to Asian interests at USD 14,5 mill. Note that the two-years-younger \"Queen Flower\" 50/2013 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 04/2026, OHBS) was sold a month ago at USD 16,5 mill. The Handysize \"Vega Falktind\" 31/2011 Fujian, China (SS/DD 03/2026) of Vega Bulk was committed at USD 8,3 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the \"T Symphony\" 32/2011 Taizhou, China (SS/DD 08/2026) was sold at USD 8,5 mill. In addition, the \"Transformer OL\" 28/2009 Shimanami, Japan (SS 11/2029, DD 01/2028) was committed to Indonesian interests at high USD 9 mill, while the \"Danship Bulker\" 28/2009 I-S, Japan (SS 02/2029, DD 02/2027) was sold a week ago at USD 8,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Eastern Mediterranean Maritime have committed their Aframax \"Hydra\" 105/2004 Sumitomo, Japan (SS 12/2025, DD 12/2025) to Far Eastern interests at USD 20,75 mill. For reference, the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Aqua Pearl\" 105/2005 Sumitomo, Japan (SS/DD 01/2026) was sold back in July at high USD 24 mill. The LR1 \"Ryvingen Sun\" 74/2007 New Century, China (SS 05/2027, DD 08/2028) of Sole Shipping was committed at USD 14,2 mill, while the sister vessel \"Chemtrans Cancale\" 73/2007 New Century, China (SS 06/2027, DD 03/2026) was committed a week ago at USD 12 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 17,000/20,000 pd range. Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd. South East Asian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into India or China were fixed around usd 17,000/20,000 pd. India trips via South Africa into China were reported at the level of usd 17,000/20,000 pd. West African trips via US Gulf into Continent were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US East Coast-US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 17,000/20,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into India were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/18,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 600K/800K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 15,500 pd for 5/8 months employment basis delivery China",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A generally quiet week for this segment. North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/16,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 14,000/16,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "West African trips via Mediterranean into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. US Gulf coastal trips were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 21,000/23,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd. A small Handysize was fixed on a period at the usd 11,100 pd basis delivery Singapore for 4/7 months employment."
    }
  },
